  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Exiling a card using its plot ability is a special action. Once you announce you\u2019re taking that action, no other player can respond by trying to remove that card from your hand.",
      "oracle_id": "00ff5598-2f7f-4e28-8b63-5ae1ce18f0c5",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a plotted card has {X} in its mana cost, you must choose 0 as the value of X when casting it without paying its mana cost.",
      "oracle_id": "00ff5598-2f7f-4e28-8b63-5ae1ce18f0c5",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you\u2019re casting a plotted card from exile without paying its mana cost, you can\u2019t choose to cast it for any other alternative costs. You can, however, pay additional costs, such as kicker costs. If the plotted card has any mandatory additional costs, those must still be paid to cast the spell.",
      "oracle_id": "00ff5598-2f7f-4e28-8b63-5ae1ce18f0c5",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Plot abilities are written \u201cPlot [cost],\u201d which means \u201cAny time you have priority during your main phase while the stack is empty, you may pay [cost] and exile this card from your hand. It becomes plotted.\u201d",
      "oracle_id": "00ff5598-2f7f-4e28-8b63-5ae1ce18f0c5",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can\u2019t cast a plotted card on the same turn it became plotted. On any future turn, you may cast that card from exile without paying its mana cost during your main phase while the stack is empty.",
      "oracle_id": "00ff5598-2f7f-4e28-8b63-5ae1ce18f0c5",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You don\u2019t choose a target for Unscrupulous Contractor\u2019s ability at the time it triggers. Rather, a second \u201creflexive\u201d ability triggers if you sacrifice a creature this way. You choose a target for that ability as it goes on the stack. Each player may respond to this triggered ability as normal. Notably, the triggered ability isn\u2019t a crime, but the reflexive triggered ability potentially is.",
      "oracle_id": "00ff5598-2f7f-4e28-8b63-5ae1ce18f0c5",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.",
      "oracle_id": "05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Adamant effects check what mana was actually spent to cast a spell. If an effect allows you to spend mana \"as though it were mana\" of any color or type, that allows you to spend mana you couldn't otherwise spend, but it doesn't change what mana you spent to cast the spell.",
      "oracle_id": "33a162f3-e781-494f-ab8f-12a84801a694",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect allows you to cast a spell without paying its mana cost, you can't choose to cast it and pay unless another rule or effect allows you to cast that spell for a cost. Similarly, you can't waive a cost reduction unless that effect says you may.",
      "oracle_id": "33a162f3-e781-494f-ab8f-12a84801a694",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an instant or sorcery spell has an adamant ability, you perform the spell's instructions in order. You don't perform the adamant instruction before the spell resolves or before any other effects printed above it.",
      "oracle_id": "33a162f3-e781-494f-ab8f-12a84801a694",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If at least three black mana was spent to cast Foreboding Fruit, you'll create a Food, even if you have another player draw two cards and lose 2 life.",
      "oracle_id": "33a162f3-e781-494f-ab8f-12a84801a694",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you copy a spell that has an adamant ability, no mana was spent to cast the copy at all, so that ability won't apply.",
      "oracle_id": "33a162f3-e781-494f-ab8f-12a84801a694",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Food is an artifact type. Even though it appears on some creatures, it's never a creature type.",
      "oracle_id": "33a162f3-e781-494f-ab8f-12a84801a694",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Some spells and abilities that create Food tokens may require targets. If each target chosen is an illegal target as that spell or ability tries to resolve, it won't resolve. You won't create any Food tokens.",
      "oracle_id": "33a162f3-e781-494f-ab8f-12a84801a694",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Whatever you do, don't eat the delicious cards.",
      "oracle_id": "33a162f3-e781-494f-ab8f-12a84801a694",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't sacrifice a Food to pay multiple costs. For example, you can't sacrifice a Food token to activate its own ability and also to activate Maraleaf Rider's ability.",
      "oracle_id": "33a162f3-e781-494f-ab8f-12a84801a694",
      "published_at": "2024-11-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If all of Silverquill Command\u2019s targets are illegal as it tries to resolve, it will do nothing.",
      "oracle_id": "6075b999-75c5-41c8-898d-ee612ba79a92",
      "published_at": "2021-04-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If at least one target is still legal as Silverquill Command tries to resolve, it will resolve and do as much as it can.",
      "oracle_id": "6075b999-75c5-41c8-898d-ee612ba79a92",
      "published_at": "2021-04-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.",
      "oracle_id": "a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each additional cost and associated mode in the text box is also preceded with a + indicator. These symbols also have no rules meaning and serve only to remind players that the listed costs are additional costs.",
      "oracle_id": "ad3e705f-da57-4eff-84d7-2072522de988",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a mode requires a target, you can select that mode only if there\u2019s a legal target available. Ignore the targeting requirements for modes you don\u2019t choose.",
      "oracle_id": "ad3e705f-da57-4eff-84d7-2072522de988",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a spell with spree is copied, the effect that creates the copy may allow you to choose new targets. You cannot choose new modes.",
      "oracle_id": "ad3e705f-da57-4eff-84d7-2072522de988",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If all targets for the chosen modes become illegal before a spell with spree resolves, the spell won\u2019t resolve and none of its effects will happen. If at least one target is still legal, the spell will resolve but will have no effect on any illegal targets.",
      "oracle_id": "ad3e705f-da57-4eff-84d7-2072522de988",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect allows you to cast a spell with spree \u201cwithout paying its mana cost,\u201d you must still choose at least one mode and pay the associated additional costs.",
      "oracle_id": "ad3e705f-da57-4eff-84d7-2072522de988",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "No matter which modes you choose, you always follow the instructions in the order they are written.",
      "oracle_id": "ad3e705f-da57-4eff-84d7-2072522de988",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "No player can cast spells or activate abilities in between the modes of a resolving spell. Any abilities that trigger won\u2019t be put onto the stack until the spell is done resolving.",
      "oracle_id": "ad3e705f-da57-4eff-84d7-2072522de988",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Spells with spree have a + (plus sign) indicator in the upper right corner of the card frame. This has no rules meaning and serves only to remind players that at least one additional cost is required to cast the spell.",
      "oracle_id": "ad3e705f-da57-4eff-84d7-2072522de988",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The mana value of a spell with spree is determined only by its mana cost (in the upper right corner of the card). It doesn\u2019t matter which modes you choose or which additional costs you pay, including any additional costs imposed by other effects.",
      "oracle_id": "ad3e705f-da57-4eff-84d7-2072522de988",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can\u2019t choose the same mode more than once.",
      "oracle_id": "ad3e705f-da57-4eff-84d7-2072522de988",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You choose the modes as you cast the spell with spree. Once modes are chosen, they can\u2019t be changed.",
      "oracle_id": "ad3e705f-da57-4eff-84d7-2072522de988",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must choose at least one of the listed modes and pay its associated additional cost in order to cast a spell with spree.",
      "oracle_id": "ad3e705f-da57-4eff-84d7-2072522de988",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
